steps.prompt:
An inquiry about a property:
{{brief}}

Start your answer with one word: HOT when they give a budget that fits, want to move within three months and have financing or cash; COLD when they are only browsing; else WARM. Then list: buying or renting, budget, area, rooms, when, financing, must-haves, and the questions to ask for what is missing.

The inquiry:
{{brief}}

What we know: {{step 1}}

Write a reply from the agent: thank them by name, answer what they asked, offer two viewing times in the next three working days (as [day, time] placeholders the agent fills in), and ask at most three of the missing questions. Warm and short, at most 140 words, in the language of the inquiry.
